French.back_translation:
Reads a fixed number of bytes from the stream.  
@param num_bytes: The number of bytes to read.  
@return: The bytes read.  
@raise EOFError: If fewer than num_bytes bytes remain in the underlying byte stream.

English:
public byte[] readBytes(int num_bytes) throws IOException {
            byte[] buffer = new byte[num_bytes];
            int bytesRead = _stream.read(buffer);
            if (bytesRead < num_bytes) {
                throw new EOFError("Not enough bytes available in the stream.");
            }
            return buffer;
        }
    }
}
